              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Dellinger (Exxon), according to Mr. Dellinger (Exxon), the Court has never affirmed an award of punitive damages under maritime law, nor held them available for unintentional conduct or oil spills."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Exxon",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-06abfc191925-0002-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 41,
                "start": 41
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Exxon, exxon recognized that a line must be drawn somewhere in assessing liability."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Exxon",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "06abfc1919250924dbc7899aee54290e0f6de6cb6debf2707241dd9ea79f6793",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-06abfc191925-0003-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 71,
                "start": 71
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Exxon, exxon has already paid $3.4\u202fbillion out of pocket for the spill; after tax credits and insurance the net amount is under $2\u202fbillion, which the petitioners argue is a substantial deterrent."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Exxon Shipping Co. (Petitioner)",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
